  "rendered": {
    "title": "Web search, agent memory continuity, and a smoother Mac update handoff",
    "intro": "Today's nightly brings two headline capabilities — built-in Aura Web Search with tiered quotas and a new Agent Continuity surface backed by memory-retrieval evidence — alongside a targeted macOS updater fix, a cloud identity resolution repair for tool callbacks, and an expanded model catalog featuring GPT-5.6.",
    "entries": [
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-1",
        "time_label": "9:47 PM",
        "started_at": "2026-07-10T04:47:33.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-07-10T04:47:33.000Z",
        "title": "Aura Web Search launches with platform-funded quotas and BYOK",
        "summary": "Brave-backed web and news search is now available to every workspace by default, funded by Aura credentials and gated by per-tier quotas, while workspaces that bring their own Brave key keep full control.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Enabled Brave-backed web and news search out of the box using Aura-funded credentials, with organization membership checks and per-user tier quotas enforced through z-billing.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "66b327d4fb25227bd6f0e0ebaaf21361829ebe2d"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Kept the platform Brave key strictly server-side: desktop requests are routed through aura-api via a new AURA_PLATFORM_TOOL_ACTION_BASE_URL, and billing calls are hard-gated to validated HTTPS endpoints before any credentials are transmitted.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "66b327d4fb25227bd6f0e0ebaaf21361829ebe2d"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Preserved optional workspace BYOK so connected org-owned Brave keys continue to live encrypted in aura-integrations and bypass the Aura-funded quota entirely.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "66b327d4fb25227bd6f0e0ebaaf21361829ebe2d"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Wired the new platform tool-action base URL into desktop validate, nightly, and stable release workflows so packaged builds resolve the correct authenticated endpoint.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "66b327d4fb25227bd6f0e0ebaaf21361829ebe2d"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-2",
        "time_label": "4:26 AM",
        "started_at": "2026-07-10T11:26:49.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-07-10T11:26:49.000Z",
        "title": "Cloud tool callbacks now resolve the caller's Aura Network identity",
        "summary": "Direct cloud tool-action callbacks that skip the session-enrichment endpoint can now correctly match the caller to an org role, unblocking Web Search and other platform tools from cold JWTs.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "When a zOS JWT identity doesn't match any org member during a role check, the server now fetches the current user from Aura Network, adds that ID to the candidate list, and caches the resolved network_user_id and profile_id on the validation cache for later callbacks.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "c394e572054a7da8c0bd3deabee38c2aaad94e81"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Added an end-to-end integration test that drives a Brave web-search tool action through a fresh cloud callback and asserts the Aura Network identity is resolved and cached.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "c394e572054a7da8c0bd3deabee38c2aaad94e81"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-3",
        "time_label": "6:39 AM",
        "started_at": "2026-07-10T13:39:51.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-07-10T13:39:51.000Z",
        "title": "macOS updater waits for shutdown before relaunching Aura",
        "summary": "The macOS auto-update flow no longer races LaunchServices — a small handoff process now waits for the current Aura process to exit before opening the updated bundle.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Replaced the immediate `open -n` relaunch with a shell handoff that polls until the parent PID disappears (up to a 30-second ceiling) and only then execs `/usr/bin/open` on the updated bundle, preventing LaunchServices from seeing the old instance as still running.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "c8307f12621f285e3f31a7e0d514e620be8aec7b"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Applied the same deferred handoff to the `/Applications` relocate-and-relaunch path so first-run installs out of a translocated location reopen cleanly after shutdown, with handoff PIDs recorded in updater diagnostics.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "c8307f12621f285e3f31a7e0d514e620be8aec7b"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-4",
        "time_label": "7:06 AM",
        "started_at": "2026-07-10T14:06:46.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-07-10T14:06:46.000Z",
        "title": "GPT-5.6 family lands with a new XHigh reasoning tier",
        "summary": "The model catalog picks up three GPT-5.6 variants and a distinct XHigh reasoning effort that sits between High and Max instead of being folded away.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Added gpt-5.6-sol, gpt-5.6-terra, and gpt-5.6-luna to the OpenAI catalog with per-model input/output and cache pricing wired into benchmark and pricing tables.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "f0aebe976bcedbc93a19ae5297b7d8df4519bd96"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Promoted `xhigh` to a first-class ReasoningEffort tier in the aura-protocol runtime request and TypeScript bindings, so GPT-5.6 exposes distinct XHigh and Max budgets instead of collapsing xhigh into high as before.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "f0aebe976bcedbc93a19ae5297b7d8df4519bd96"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Reframed the ReasoningEffort documentation as a provider-neutral superset, clarifying that Aura Router maps Minimal to `none` for current OpenAI models and translates each tier into the provider's native control.",
            "commit_shas": [
